Introduction

Oracle Data Guard is one of the key technologies used to provide database-level disaster recovery and high availability.

In this environment, I configured an Oracle 19c Physical Standby Database and enabled Active Data Guard, allowing the standby database to remain open for read-only workloads while Redo Apply continues.

The environment used in this setup:

component                           value 
primary database                    PRIMCA
standby database                    STDBYCA
Oracle Version                      19.32.0
Database Type                       Physical Standby 
Storage                             ASM
Protection Mode                     MaxPerformance
Duplicate Method                    RMAN Active Duplicate


The overall flow was:

primary database -> RMAN Active Duplicate -> Physical Standby -> Redo Transport -> Redo Apply -> READ ONLY WITH APPLY

